   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">(i) Status of nationally determined contributions, national mid-century strategies and NAPs communicated to the UNFCCC in 6 EaP countries; (ii) Level of institutional capacities in the six EaP countries for the implementation of the Paris Agreement; (iii) Level of alignment with EU acquis as provided by bilateral agreements with EU and in the framework of Energy Community Treaty; (iv) Level of mobilization of new climate finance resources by countries (including under NIF/NIP) since the start of the project, EUR.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">NA</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Assist the Government with NDC revision
2) Develop LT- LEDS strategy in accordance with the roadmap and facilitate its submission to the relevant state authorities
3) Assist the Government to identify key criteria for selecting emitter enterprises (installation-level MRV system) in energy and industry sectors based on international or EU experience
4) Conduct in-depth analysis of the current legislative base on GHG MRV system and identify whether necessary updates and/or changes should be made to the legislative acts or new draft legislative act/s regulating MRV activities should be developed
5) Develop guidelines on mainstreaming climate change concept into the energy and agriculture policies
6) Provide recommendations on how to apply Climate budget tagging (CBT) and the perspectives of applying CBT methodology on the national budgeting system.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Final NDC report is finalized and submitted to the Government for approval. 
2) Final report is under preparation and Government approval expected in March 2022
3) The reports are finalized and submitted to the line ministries for review. Presentation to the Government expected in mid-2022
4) The identification report on necessary updates or changes to the legislative acts was submitted to the national stakeholders, and final summary will be presented during the workshop planned for the mid-2022
5) The Guidelines on agriculture sector has been finalized, and The &#x201c;Guidelines on mainstreaming climate change and gender concept into the energy policy&#x201d; is expected to be finalized by the end of February 2022
6) The report on how to apply climate budget tagging (CBT) and the perspectives of applying CBT methodology on the national budgeting system submitted to the Government for review</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Develop LT- LEDS strategy in accordance with the roadmap and facilitate its submission to the relevant state authorities.
2) Assist the Government to identify key criteria for selecting emitter enterprises (installation-level MRV system) in energy and industry sectors based on international or EU experience.
3) Conduct in-depth analysis of the current legislative base on GHG MRV system and identify whether necessary updates and/or changes should be made to the legislative acts or new draft legislative act/s regulating MRV activities should be developed.
4) Develop guidelines on mainstreaming climate change and gender concepts into the energy and agriculture policies.
5) Provide recommendations on how to apply Climate budget tagging (CBT) and the perspectives of applying CBT methodology on the national budgeting system.
6) Conduct piloting exercise on climate budget tagging (CBT) in Azerbaijan in consultation with the Ministry of Finance and its relevant institutions.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Final report on LT-LEDS has been finalized and submitted to the Government of Azerbaijan for review and approval. 
2) The final combined report is finalized and was . presented to the Government.
3) The identification report on necessary updates to the legislative acts was submitted to the Government, and final summary was presented during the workshop in 2022.
4) Both Guidelines have been finalized and submitted to the GoA.
5) The report on how to apply climate budget tagging (CBT) and the perspectives of applying CBT methodology on the national budgeting system submitted to the Government for review.
6) The hiring processes of international and national experts have been finalized and the final piloting exercise will be presented to the GoA in year 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Provide guidance and technical support to the government on NDC update
2) Develop a roadmap on preparation the LEDS (Low emission development strategy)
3) Develop a gap analysis report, including the recommendations on how to improve the current MRV (monitoring, reporting and verification) system 
4) Prepare a gap analysis on the legislative alignment with EU on climate change
5) Develop recommendations on mainstreaming climate change into the priority sectors
6) Develop recommendations to integrate climate finance into budgeting process and to implement Climate Budget Tagging (CBT) in Azerbaijan</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Template on updating NDC developed
2) LEDS Roadmap finalized and company on developing LEDS hired
3) Gap analysis report is in the process of preparation by EAA (Environment Agency of Austria) hired by UNDP IRH
4) Gap analysis report on the legislative alignment with EU developed by EAA (Environment Agency of Austria) hired by UNDP IRH
5) Recommendations on mainstreaming climate change developed
6) Recommendations to integrate climate finance into budgeting process and implement Climate Budget Tagging (CBT) in Azerbaijan developed by the local consultant</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
